BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art at the Kent 2026: Throughlines
DTSTART:20261011T100000
DTEND:20261011T170000
DTSTAMP:20261015T153851Z
UID:4304fa6bc336806c668265abe82e0f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Art at the Kent’s widely anticipated 2026 exhibition\, Throu
 ghlines \, gathers the work of 20 contemporary Vermont artists from Friday
 \, September 11\, through Sunday\, October 11\, 2026. Visitors can view th
 ese works within the rambling historic structures of the Kents’ Corner S
 tate Historic Site—as well as on the surrounding grounds. With multidisc
 iplinary works of art reflecting themes of place\, community\, and connect
 ion\, Throughlines celebrates the making of art using myriad materials and
  many ways of seeing\, key characteristics at the heart of our exhibitions
  for the past two decades. Various interpretations of the theme\, both ove
 rt and subtle\, are evidenced in the diverse work of the exhibiting artist
 s. In Throughlines\, marks made in one medium evoke rich relationships wit
 h those made in another\, deepening the viewer’s appreciation for resona
 nce. Throughout the Kent\, with its own storied patina tying the present t
 o the past\, the connections made between art and building and visitor ech
 o the ties between time and place and community as our audience discovers 
 a unique sense of shared roots and different perspectives. Creative expres
 sion becomes a throughline for appreciating life’s odysseys\, preserving
  a sense of possibility\, and navigating the way forward. Art at the Kent 
 also hosts a variety of associated events that visitors can experience\, i
 ncluding Words Out Loud\, the popular Sunday afternoon reading series (Sep
 tember 13\, 20\, and 27) at the historic meetinghouse nearby\, the Old Wes
 t Church. All programs can be found on the website including multiple arti
 st talks\, demonstrations of mokuhanga (a Japanese printmaking technique) 
 and paper folding\, as well as a presentation on the history and repair of
  antique typewriters. More information and a full listing of these and oth
 er events can be found on the Art at the Kent Events page. Art at the Kent
  is a program of Historic Kents’ Corner\, Inc.\, in partnership with the
  Vermont State Curator’s Office and the Vermont Division for Historic Pr
 eservation. For nearly two decades\, contemporary art exhibitions have bee
 n presented to engage and challenge audiences by providing unusual exposur
 e to mid-nineteenth-century architecture enhanced by the art of our time. 
 The Kents’ Corner State Historic Site is administered by the Vermont Div
 ision for Historic Preservation. Open to all. Donations encouraged. Exhibi
 tion Dates: September 11–October 11\, 2026 Every week through Oct 11\, 2
 026.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Kents’ Corner State Historic Site\, 7 Old West Church Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/art-at-the
 -kent-2026-throughlines-07-08-2026-11-38-46
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spitfire Shipwreck Virtual Reality Experience
DTSTART:20261013T100000
DTEND:20261013T120000
DTSTAMP:20261015T153851Z
UID:24519247fac45df00f5ee88ac5aa9f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Want to know what it’s like to explore an underwater shipwre
 ck? Dive into the Lake Champlain Maritime Museum’s virtual reality tour 
 of Spitfire\, a 1776 gunboat that sank during the American retreat from Va
 lcour Bay. Using thousands of photos\, sonar images\, and videos of the wr
 eck\, we created a detailed\, 3-dimensional model which Champlain College 
 students transformed into this virtual reality dive. Stop by Fragments: Vo
 ices of the American Revolution on Lake Champlain and experience it for yo
 urself! Accessibility: From the flexi-pave path\, there is one wheelchair 
 accessible entrance to Fragments on the north side of the building. The ex
 hibit space is fully ADA compliant. Every week through Oct 15\, 2026.\n\nS
 ources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lake Champlain Maritime Museum\, 4472 Basin Harbor Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/spitfire-s
 hipwreck-virtual-reality-experience-14-09-2026-14-34-29
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Living Song
DTSTART:20261015T173000
DTEND:20261015T193000
DTSTAMP:20261015T153851Z
UID:b0a14a8d8239a9838c75f902802199@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:What do we love about singing with others? Connection\, joy\, 
 catharsis—and the feeling of creating something together. In this welcom
 ing circle-singing workshop\, we’ll explore structured\, highly supporte
 d vocal improvisation as we listen\, respond\, and find a shared musical f
 low. New to circle singing? Wonderful. Experienced? You’re welcome\, too
 . No experience necessary—just bring your voice and a willingness to pla
 y. Come sing\, connect\, and co-create a living song. Led by teaching arti
 st Kristin Marchilena.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Flynn\, 153 Main St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/a-living-s
 ong-06-10-2026-14-59-57
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Elizabeth Chang and Jiayan Sun
DTSTART:20261015T120000
DTEND:20261015T133000
DTSTAMP:20261015T153851Z
UID:6f1c9f29381b39891f1adf5a0e429b@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Violinist Elizabeth Chang\, Artistic Director of the Green Mou
 ntain Chamber Music Festival\, joins Steinway pianist Jiayan Sun for a pro
 gram spanning the Classical and early Romantic eras: Mozart's Violin Sonat
 a in B-Flat Major\, K. 454\, Beethoven's Violin Sonata No. 8 in G Major\, 
 Op. 30\, No. 3\, and Schubert's sweeping Fantasy for Violin and Piano. An 
 intimate afternoon showcasing exceptional musicians at the height of their
  artistry. This is a free concert.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Cathedral Church of St. Paul\, 2 Cherry Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/elizabeth-
 chang-and-jiayan-sun-21-09-2026-18-55-03
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gap Year Information Night
DTSTART:20261015T180000
DTEND:20261015T190000
DTSTAMP:20261015T153851Z
UID:27aa4ba43edbd3b327ca3e7dc6e894@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The transition after high school has always involved big decis
 ions\, and research shows that students who take an intentional gap year a
 fter high school emerge with real-world skills\, greater self-confidence\,
  and a clearer sense of purpose. Julia Rogers\, a local gap year counselor
  and nationally recognized expert on experiential education\, will share h
 ow gap years help students prepare for what’s ahead. She’ll outline ho
 w families can make can make a gap year possible\, highlight the wide rang
 e of opportunities students are pursuing\, and explain why more colleges a
 nd employers are recognizing the benefits of the gap year option.\n\nSourc
 es: Vermont Public
LOCATION:South Burlington Library\, 180 Market St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/gap-year-i
 nformation-night-30-09-2026-14-44-32
END:VEVENT
