BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How the Bicycle Came to Vermont
DTSTART:20261015T183000
DTEND:20261015T200000
DTSTAMP:20261015T153851Z
UID:eb2f0357448cd933863bdfea2fec66@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an exciting and informational evening as Luis A. V
 ivanco\, Professor and Chair of Anthropology at UVM\, walks us through the
  history of the bicycle and how it entered into Vermont life. Fletcher Fre
 e Library\, Main Reading Room Please RSVP - The event is free\, but we nee
 d to know how many to expect! Luis Vivanco is a long-time cyclist and has 
 combined his love for two wheels with his areas of expertise in many ways.
  Take a look through his website The Illustrated Wheel (illustratedwheel.c
 om) to learn more\, and we highly suggest perusing his bike history comics
  for some entertaining insight on the evening's topic.\n\nSources: Vermont
  Public
LOCATION:Fletcher Free Library\, 235 College St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/how-the-bi
 cycle-came-to-vermont-29-09-2026-17-38-05
END:VEVENT
