BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Community Storytelling
DTSTART:20261015T180000
DTEND:20261015T200000
DTSTAMP:20261015T153851Z
UID:3b75844c74c9e9414f085d68245e5a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:What does it mean to belong—to a place\, a community\, a cre
 ative practice\, or one another? Join your neighbors and fellow creatives 
 for a generative workshop exploring belonging through storytelling. Throug
 h dynamic writing exercises\, embodied exploration\, and collective story 
 sharing\, we’ll mine our lived experiences for new material\, perspectiv
 es\, and possibilities. Together\, we’ll explore how telling\, listening
  to\, and witnessing stories can deepen our creative practice and build a 
 sense of connection and community. No experience with writing or storytell
 ing necessary—just curiosity and a willingness to explore. Come ready to
  experiment\, reflect\, and create in community. Led by teaching artists F
 erene Paris & Gina Stevensen\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Flynn\, 153 Main St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-art-of
 -community-storytelling-06-10-2026-14-29-26
END:VEVENT
